==============================================================================
§2  Smoothing laws (T2)
==============================================================================
t = 14.134725141734693, sigma = 1/2, dps = 60
N ladder: [100, 200, 400, 800, 1000, 1600, 3200, 6400, 12800, 25600, 51200, 102400]

Master law (derived from Abel summation + Euler-Maclaurin; every term checked below):
   S_N^phi - zeta = N^{1-s} J(phi) + phi(0) zeta(s) + R_N,
   J(phi) = int_0^1 phi(u) u^{-s} du,   R_N = O(N^{-sigma}) = O(N^{-1/2}).
The sqrt(N) term is governed by u=0 (through J), NOT by phi(1).

